#import "../macros.typ": *

The eight classes below are the 1PI functions of ghost number 1 with $sum_j dim Phi_j <= 5$ and exactly one vertex $Dbrk_1$ (@eq:V-delta); all other vertices are those of $S_0$ (@sec:m-oneloop). $Dbrk_1$ couples a ghost, a physical fermion and its sterile partner through $slh(p)$ or $slh(p)'$.

*Which diagrams contribute.* In the first kind of diagram the external ghost sits on $Dbrk_1$ and both fermion legs of the vertex are internal. In each term of @eq:V-delta one line next to the vertex is the sterile component, and the vertex with this sterile propagator is the scalar insertion $plus.minus i Tg^a hat(q)^2 \/ q^2$ of @eq:m-sterile on a physical fermion line. At zero ghost momentum the two terms of @eq:V-delta cancel between physical neighbours (@eq:m-tree-WI, @eq:g1_cVVV_cVVVV-q0), so diagrams of this kind with $dg(G) = 0$ vanish under $Top(0)$. In the second kind the ghost of $Dbrk_1$ is internal and ends on a ghost--gauge vertex @eq:V-ghost that carries a non-abelian external ghost. $Dbrk_1$ then sits at an external fermion leg. The term of @eq:V-delta with the sterile leg external carries a hatted external momentum and can only give an evanescent pole (@sec:g1_cFF); the term with the sterile leg internal gives $hat(k)^2$. These internal-ghost diagrams occur in $gh overline(Psi) Psi$, $gh overline(Psi) Psi A$, $gh overline(Psi) Psi H$ and $gh gh overline(srcF) Psi$.

*What is extracted.* The graphs of a class with legs $Phi_1 dots Phi_n$ sum to $i thin (Dbrk_1 dot Gamma)^((1))_(Phi_1 dots Phi_n)$. Each graph $G$ of degree $dg(G) >= 0$ is expanded with $Top(dg(G))$ (@sec:integrals), and two quantities are read off @eq:N0N1. The pole $N_0$ is evanescent wherever it is non-zero; it must cancel against the tree vertex $bop_d delta S^((1))$ built from the ghost-number-0 results (check of @sec:m-oneloop). The finite part is $Pphys N_1$, the coefficient of $eta\/ep$ with hatted external quantities set to zero. It gives $X_(1; Phi_1 dots Phi_n) = lf thin Pphys N_1$, the vertex function (@sec:dictionary) of the local functional $X_1$ on these legs, so that $V_(bop Delta S^((1))) = -X_1$ (@eq:m-X1). Only diagrams with $dg(G) >= 0$ and an internal sterile line next to $Dbrk_1$ contribute to $X_1$ (@eq:m-PG). $X_1$ is expanded in the basis $N_beta$ of @tab:Nbasis.

*Notation common to the eight classes.* $D_MUV = 1\/(k^2 - MUV^2)$ is the denominator of the expansion @eq:uv-expansion. $S_f^((r))$ and $C^((r))_"ad"$ are the group invariants of @tab:invariants, and the closed fermion loops give the sums over all multiplets
$ S^((r)) = S^((r))_"lh" + S^((r))_"rh" = sum_(f in {Q, U, D, L, E}) S^((r))_f , quad quad S^((G)) = 2 gs^2, quad S^((W)) = 2 gw^2, quad S^((B)) = 10/3 gy^2 , $
with $S^((r))_"lh"$, $S^((r))_"rh"$ of @eq:SLR. The parity-odd parts are expressed through the anomaly traces $D^(a b c)$ of @eq:Dabc only.

*Functions without a one-loop diagram.* Besides $gh gh overline(srcF) Psi$ and its conjugate, the ghost-number-1 functions with a BRST source are $gh gh tilde(srcA)$, $gh gh tilde(srcA) A$, $gh gh gh srcC$, $gh gh srcH^dagger H$ and $gh gh H^dagger srcH$. None of the five has a one-loop diagram with a $Dbrk_1$ vertex (@sec:g1_ccRF), so $X_1$ vanishes in these classes at one loop; this gives five of the eight existence conditions of @sec:normalisation.
